#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""claude-classifier-docker — run Claude Code in a locked-down Docker container.

(Generated from ZIS claude-docker by Classifier/claude-classifier-docker/make.py: its own config and policy; the sign-in and images of claude-docker.)

Usage:
  claude-classifier-docker                  Claude in this terminal, on the local folder
  claude-classifier-docker DIR              ... on DIR instead
  claude-classifier-docker --gui [DIR]      ... in a separate "Claude window" with Session,
                                 Review and Help menus
  claude-classifier-docker --shell [DIR]    a bash shell in the same container, not Claude

What a session can see and do (hardening of 2026-09-28):
  - The launch folder is mounted READ-ONLY at /workspace. --write SUBDIR makes
    one subfolder writable (repeatable; "." means all of it).
  - Credential-looking files in it (and those in ~/.config/claude-classifier-docker/hide.txt)
    show up empty, and the launch lists them.
  - Network: only Anthropic and the hosts in ~/.config/claude-classifier-docker/allowed-hosts.txt,
    through a proxy outside the container. No DNS, no route to this machine.
  - Its own Claude config, rebuilt fresh each session, never your ~/.claude.
  - Memory a session writes is held for your review (claude-classifier-docker --memory).
  - Policy it cannot change: prompts only, no hooks, no MCP servers, no claude.ai
    connectors, no artifacts (claude-classifier-docker --policy).

Options for a launch:
  --write SUBDIR        make SUBDIR of the launch folder writable (repeatable)
  --allow-host HOST     also allow HOST for this launch only (repeatable)
  --brief-file FILE     instructions given out of sight (appended system prompt)
  --prompt-file FILE    an initial prompt, shown as the first message
  --settings-file FILE  extra Claude Code settings for this session only
  --model NAME|N        a different model for this session only
  --continue            reopen the latest Docker session, with its launch settings
  --resume [ID]         reopen a chosen session (a list if no ID)

Commands run on this machine (never from inside a container):
  --allow HOST [--keep] let running sessions reach HOST now; --keep saves it
  --memory              review memory changes sessions have made
  --policy [edit]       show (or edit) the policy the container can't change
  --models              list the models and choose your default
  --default-model NAME  set your default without the menu
  --upgrade             rebuild the images with the newest Claude Code
  --selftest            check the protections one by one

The launch folder is DIR if given, else CLAUDE_CLASSIFIER_DOCKER_WORKSPACE (ZIS sets it),
else ~/.config/claude-classifier-docker/default-workspace — the local folder, i.e. where ZIS
is installed (the install writes it). Your home folder, the
Windows profile folder and whole drives are refused.
"""

